{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38345372",
      "title": "The Spread Operator",
      "sourceHash": "f4b9d0cfd07542a7c2f184abd6be1479038c7c63393a8b24d147732eb6ea50aa",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.5,
          "en": "Now, the other crucial concept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.5,
          "end": 7.11,
          "en": "that's related to arrays and objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.11,
          "end": 10.65,
          "en": "about which you should know is the special spread operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.65,
          "end": 12.99,
          "en": "that exists in JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.99,
          "end": 15.81,
          "en": "For that, let's for example, say that we wanna merge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.81,
          "end": 19.05,
          "en": "this hobbies list with another hobbies list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.05,
          "end": 20.25,
          "en": "In this case, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.25,
          "end": 22.623,
          "en": "another list that only contains one item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.7,
          "end": 26.76,
          "en": "If I would want to create a merged list, I could do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.76,
          "end": 30.12,
          "en": "by creating a new list with the square brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.12,
          "end": 33.24,
          "en": "And then, I could use the special spread operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.24,
          "end": 35.19,
          "en": "which looks like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.19,
          "end": 37.26,
          "en": "Three dots, yes, it looks weird,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.26,
          "end": 41.25,
          "en": "but this is JavaScript syntax using three dots,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.25,
          "end": 44.28,
          "en": "and then the name of the first array you wanna merge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 44.28,
          "end": 45.39,
          "en": "into this new array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.39,
          "end": 47.43,
          "en": "For example, hobbies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.43,
          "end": 50.76,
          "en": "These three dots will pull out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.76,
          "end": 52.83,
          "en": "all the elements of this array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.83,
          "end": 56.07,
          "en": "so sports and cooking in this case, and add them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.07,
          "end": 60.393,
          "en": "as separate, comma separated values to this new list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.44,
          "end": 65.4,
          "en": "If I would just add hobbies like this, and new hobbies",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 65.4,
          "end": 68.97,
          "en": "like this, I would get a new array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.97,
          "end": 70.38,
          "en": "which when output",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.38,
          "end": 74.61,
          "en": "to the console, will actually look like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.61,
          "end": 78.60300000000001,
          "en": "Now, it's an array with two nested arrays inside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.74,
          "end": 83.133,
          "en": "This might sometimes be what you want, but often, it's not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.36,
          "end": 87.51,
          "en": "If I instead use the three dots",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.51,
          "end": 92.4,
          "en": "in front of the arrays to use this spread operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.4,
          "end": 95.49000000000001,
          "en": "I will pull out the values from these arrays,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.49000000000001,
          "end": 98.703,
          "en": "and add them as standalone values to this array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.78,
          "end": 103.47,
          "en": "And with that, if I reload this new array I get,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 103.47,
          "end": 105.87,
          "en": "now does not contain nested arrays,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.87,
          "end": 109.113,
          "en": "but instead, the values from the merged arrays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 110.07,
          "end": 112.02000000000001,
          "en": "And that's what the spread operator does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 112.02000000000001,
          "end": 116.34,
          "en": "It pulls out values from an array, and adds them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.34,
          "end": 121.2,
          "en": "as separate, comma separated values to a new array here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 121.2,
          "end": 123.6,
          "en": "And we will indeed use this spread operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 123.6,
          "end": 125.1,
          "en": "from time to time in this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.1,
          "end": 127.45,
          "en": "And therefore, you should also know about this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.64,
          "end": 132.39,
          "en": "You can also not just use this spread operator on arrays,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.39,
          "end": 134.52,
          "en": "but also an objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 134.52,
          "end": 138.69,
          "en": "For example, if I have my extended user object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.69,
          "end": 142.68,
          "en": "where I also have the isAdmin flag, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.68,
          "end": 147.06,
          "en": "a property named isAdmin, which stores a Boolean value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.06,
          "end": 151.35,
          "en": "And I now wanna merge in the properties from the other user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.35,
          "end": 153.9,
          "en": "Now, for that, I can again use the spread operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.9,
          "end": 158.31,
          "en": "because it's also available in objects, and spread my user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 158.31,
          "end": 161.763,
          "en": "with help of these three dots into this extended user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.69,
          "end": 165.87,
          "en": "Here, the spread operator will pull out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.87,
          "end": 169.86,
          "en": "all the key value pairs from this object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 169.86,
          "end": 173.553,
          "en": "and add them as key value pairs to that object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 174.48,
          "end": 178.62,
          "en": "The offer, if I console.log this extendedUser now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.62,
          "end": 183.27,
          "en": "I'll get a new user which has this isAdmin key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 183.27,
          "end": 186.03,
          "en": "but which also has these key value pairs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 186.03,
          "end": 187.293,
          "en": "from this user here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 189.09,
          "end": 192.663,
          "en": "All thanks to this spread operator, to the three dots.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}